id: pm-web-se1p
title: Adopt pm CLI 2026.10.30 explicit history order in the pm-toolchain bump (PR 289)
description: "The pm-toolchain Dependabot bump to @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.30 changed the CLI history contract (GH-1617): display order is now explicit and consistent across projections, compact output arrives newest-first with an order label, and a --order option was added. Track the pm-web migration: the normalizer fixture in the projection test, the explicit order request in the history page reader, and the unrelated src/server.js log line seen in CI."
type: Chore
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: dependencies,"gh:unbraind/pm-web#289",migration,sdk
created_at: "2026-11-03T10:24:56.230Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-10T22:30:56.470Z"
author: toolchain-web-1103
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-03T10:25:08.351Z",toolchain-web-1103,"Root cause 1 (test fixture pinned old CLI behaviour): pm-cli GH-1617 (2026.10.30, Fixed) made history display order explicit. 'pm history <id> --compact' now returns newest-first rows with order:\"newest_first\"; the old versions returned an unlabeled oldest-first stream. The projection test fixture reversed compact_history and relabeled it newest_first, which under the new CLI yields oldest-first rows mislabeled newest_first; normalizeItemHistory correctly returns them newest-first and the deepEqual against the chronological expectation fails. The production reader readItemHistoryPage is unaffected because it consumes --full output (default oldest_first with an explicit label) and the normalizer honors the label. Plan: update the fixture to the new delivery contract and additionally request --order oldest_first explicitly in the page reader so the route contract no longer depends on the per-mode default."
  "2026-11-03T10:29:00.473Z",toolchain-web-1103,"Fix 1 (production hardening): readRows in src/services/item-history.ts now passes --order oldest_first on every host history read. The route contract (ItemHistoryPage.order = oldest_first) previously relied on the --full projection default; GH-1617 made order an explicit host choice, so pm-web requests its contract instead of inheriting a mode default that upstream could change. Verified through the real SDK dispatcher: the route-level pagination tests (bounded pages, stale cursors, 60 adversarial append schedules) pass on 2026.10.30 with the flag."
  "2026-11-03T10:29:02.345Z",toolchain-web-1103,"Fix 2 (test fixture updated to the new contract, intent kept): test/item-history-projection.test.ts asserted the normalizer against a fixture built by reversing compact_history, which assumed the pre-2026.10.30 unlabeled oldest-first compact stream. Under 2026.10.30 the compact projection arrives newest-first with order:newest_first, so the reversed fixture became oldest-first rows mislabeled newest_first and the normalizer correctly returned newest-first. The fixture now asserts the delivered order label (newest_first), checks normalized indices 1..4, and feeds the complementary oldest-first fixture; the timestamp-tie fixture derives from the oldest-first rows so delivered order still survives ties. No assertion was deleted; the refusal, tie and transport-failure coverage is unchanged."
  "2026-11-03T10:29:25.937Z",toolchain-web-1103,"Investigated the 'Cannot find module src/server.js' line in the CI log: it is not caused by this bump. It appears in the failing toolchain run and in green main runs alike, printed by test/server-bootstrap.test.ts ('the extension starts, probes and stops PostgreSQL servers and propagates child startup failures'), which deliberately asserts src/server.js is absent (the source wrapper has no emitted server sibling) and then expects the shipped host's web command to fail with exit code 1 through that missing sibling. No action needed; recorded here per the brief."
  "2026-11-03T10:31:00.897Z",toolchain-web-1103,"Hosted-facing views check: the history panel and the item detail timeline consume only pm-web's own /pm/history route, whose ItemHistoryPage/HistoryResponse contract is a literal order:'oldest_first' (src/services/item-history.ts and public/src/api-types.ts). The frontend's reverse-to-display logic therefore relies on the server contract, not on the CLI's projection defaults, and GH-1617 cannot change it; the server now also requests oldest_first explicitly from the host. No frontend change needed."
  "2026-11-03T11:14:53.807Z",toolchain-web-1103,"Gates: node --test test/item-history-projection.test.ts 7/7 pass (A/B verified: the new explicit-order regression test fails without the src fix). Full npm test: 884 tests, 881 pass; the 3 failures are host npm policy, not code (EALLOWSCRIPTS refusal of project-scoped installs spawned by tests). Reran the affected files with NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG=/dev/null (CI-equivalent env): the old-version normalization suite passes and catalog-install-e2e passes 3/3. typecheck pass, lint pass, changelog:check up to date, dist rebuilt and committed. No upstream regressions found in pm-cli 2026.10.30 history behaviour: the compact projection now labels its order explicitly and the normalizer handles the label correctly."
  "2026-11-10T22:30:56.469Z",codex-smallfix2-1110,"Follow-up compatibility evidence from the capped full gate on the authorized-read branch: the legacy npm history matrix failed with EALLOWSCRIPTS while installing CLI 2026.10.20 into a fresh prefix with ignore-scripts. The npm diagnostic says allow-scripts is not permitted for project-scoped installs. The fixture copies inherited npm configuration without clearing npm_config_allow_scripts case-insensitively. Investigate the child-environment sanitizer using synthetic configuration while preserving the version and history assertions. The full gate finished 963 tests: 961 passed, one failed and one cancelled; the other case was a catalog-install test deadline tracked on pm-web-qdhx."
